  "en": "# PG Unit Hello Course A: Self-Care & Daily Routine Experience\n\n## Course Overview\n\n### Course Type\n\nSelf-Care & Daily Routine Experience\n\n### Course Purpose\n\nThis one-lesson Unit Hello course helps PG children experience a soft arrival routine. The focus is not independent self-care, but feeling welcomed, noticing personal belongings, and beginning to understand that school has safe places for children and their things.\n\n---\n\n# Lesson 1: I Come to School\n\n## Lesson Outcome\n\n### 1. Cognitive Objectives\n\nChildren begin to notice a simple school arrival sequence: come in, find teacher, place bag or cup, and come to the mat.\n\n### 2. Skill-based Objectives\n\nChildren practise adult-supported arrival actions such as carrying or pointing to a bag, placing a cup, sitting briefly, or moving toward the teacher.\n\n### 3. Affective Objectives\n\nChildren begin to feel safe and welcomed during the first school routine.\n\n## HighScope KDI Alignment\n\n### Domain: B. Social and Emotional Development\n\n**Items:** 9. Emotions; 12. Building relationships\n\n**How We Support:** Children are supported through the emotional work of arriving at school by staying close to a caring adult, accepting comfort, and seeing that the teacher is a safe person.\n\n### Domain: C. Physical Development and Health\n\n**Items:** 19. Personal care\n\n**How We Support:** Children take part in very early personal routine actions such as placing a bag, finding a cup, or coming to a mat, with full adult support.\n\n## Theme Story Context\n\nThe teacher welcomes children with a calm class mascot. The mascot comes to school, finds the teacher, puts its bag in a safe place, and sits near the group.\n\nChildren may copy one small action or simply watch while staying close to the teacher or caregiver.\n\n## Light Theme Language\n\n```text\nhello\nschool\nteacher\nbag\ncup\nmat\ncome\nsit\n```\n\n## Teacher Routine Language\n\n```text\nHello.\nCome in.\nBag here.\nCup here.\nCome to teacher.\nSit here.\nAll done.\nGood coming to school.\n```\n\n## Suggested Activities / Games\n\n### 1. Bag Finds Home\n\nChildren bring, point to, or watch their bag being placed in a stable classroom spot.\n\n### 2. Cup Here\n\nChildren place or point to their cup with teacher support.\n\n### 3. Come to the Mat\n\nChildren move toward the mat, sit briefly, or stay near the teacher while the group settles.\n",
  "zh": "# PG Unit Hello Course A：自理与日常常规体验\n\n## 课程概览\n\n### 课程类型\n\n自理与日常常规体验\n\n### 课程目的\n\n这节 Unit Hello 课程帮助 PG 儿童体验柔和的入园常规。重点不是独立自理，而是感到被欢迎，注意自己的个人物品，并开始理解学校里有安全的位置可以放置儿童和他们的物品。\n\n---\n\n# 第一课：我来到学校\n\n## 课程目标\n\n### 1. 认知目标\n\n儿童开始注意简单的入园顺序：进来、找到教师、放置书包或水杯，然后来到垫子区域。\n\n### 2. 技能目标\n\n儿童练习成人支持下的入园动作，例如拿着或指向书包、放置水杯、短暂坐下，或朝教师移动。\n\n### 3. 情感目标\n\n儿童在第一个学校常规中开始感到安全和被欢迎。\n\n## HighScope KDI\n\n### 领域：B. 社会性与情绪发展\n\n**项目：** 9. 情绪；12. 建立关系\n\n**支持方式：** 儿童通过靠近关爱的成人、接受安抚，并看见教师是安全的人，获得入园情绪适应的支持。\n\n### 领域：C. 身体发展与健康\n\n**项目：** 19. 个人照护\n\n**支持方式：** 儿童在充分成人支持下参与非常早期的个人常规动作，例如放书包、找到水杯或来到垫子。\n\n## 主题故事情境\n\n教师用平静的班级吉祥物欢迎儿童。吉祥物来到学校，找到教师，把书包放在安全位置，然后坐到集体附近。\n\n儿童可以模仿一个小动作，也可以只是观察，并靠近教师或照护者。\n\n## 轻量主题语言\n\n```text\nhello\nschool\nteacher\nbag\ncup\nmat\ncome\nsit\n```\n\n## 教师常规语言\n\n```text\nHello.\nCome in.\nBag here.\nCup here.\nCome to teacher.\nSit here.\nAll done.\nGood coming to school.\n```\n\n## 建议活动 / 游戏\n\n### 1. 书包回家\n\n儿童把书包带到、指向或观看书包被放到稳定的教室位置。\n\n### 2. 水杯放这里\n\n儿童在教师支持下放置或指向自己的水杯。\n\n### 3. 来到垫子\n\n儿童朝垫子移动、短暂坐下，或在集体安顿时靠近教师。\n"
